  month = jan,
  day = {13},
  howpublished = {Massachusetts Historical Society, collection item 557},
  url = {https://www.masshist.org/database/557},
  urldate = {2026-09-18},
  note = {Source for the claim's assertion by the people it concerned. The petition reads: “That your Petitioners apprehend that they have, in common with all other Men, a natural and unalienable right to that freedom, which the great Parent of the Universe hath bestowed equally on all Mankind, and which they have never forfeited by any compact or agreement whatever.” Dated 13 January 1777, under six months after the Declaration. **The legislature did not act on it**, and it is one of at least five antislavery petitions brought by Black petitioners to the Massachusetts government between 1773 and 1777 — so the argument preceded the Declaration and the Declaration gave it a text, which is the narrower thing the book says. Read from secondary transcriptions of the petition's text, several of them reproducing the same passage identically; the manuscript in the Society's database was not opened. Agent-verified 2026-09-18.}
}

