  urldate     = {2026-09-13},
  note        = {Bundesgerichtshof, Third Criminal Senate, on appeal from Landgericht Stuttgart (judgment of 29 September 2006). Reported at BGHSt 51, 244; NJW 2007, 1602; NStZ 2007, 466. The defendant sold stickers, badges and similar items to the punk scene bearing National Socialist symbols crossed out, smashed or otherwise negated. Held that using a proscribed organization's symbol in a depiction whose content plainly and unmistakably expresses opposition to the organization and rejection of its ideology does not run counter to the protective purpose of \S\,86a and therefore falls outside the offence, the opposition having to be recognizable at first glance. The conviction was set aside and the defendant acquitted. Agent-verified 2026-09-13 against the court's own press release and the reported headnote.},
